{
  "what": "Addresses the Agent's page and the desktop both read, so that the two sides are tested against the same list (the Agent's tests in app/tests/unit/backup.test.ts and the desktop's in src/backup/tests.rs). `own` are addresses a person may have typed into a provider or the image, video and audio service: an undo puts every one of them back exactly as it was, whatever it holds. `backup` are addresses as a backup and a restore see them: `cleaned` is what the page writes into a backup and what the desktop makes of it when it is restored (`changed` says something was taken out: a name and password, a fragment, a parameter that is not the version of an API), and `comesBack` says whether the desktop brings `cleaned` back at all (an address that is not a web address does not, and its key goes with it).",
